  "content": "{\"workspace_id\": \"incident-lens\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"public_summary\": {\"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"title\": \"Service observation window\", \"started_at\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"observed_symptoms\": [\"Request latency and error rate observation window\"], \"services\": [\"gateway\", \"backend\", \"postgres\", \"redis\", \"payment\"]}, \"budgets\": {\"max_rounds\": 8, \"max_tool_calls\": 32, \"max_llm_calls\": 48, \"max_wall_seconds\": 5400.0, \"max_tokens\": null}, \"round_index\": 4, \"findings\": [{\"finding_id\": \"gap-ab9306127a08376f1b35c6540299991c28696c0fd09a18e2befe92c341a24fa8\", \"task_id\": \"task-01-postgres-health\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"role\": \"database\", \"claim\": \"No evidence for this query; this is not proof of healthy behavior. [{\\\"call_id\\\": \\\"call-a01f081ac3094221ab7b5e090ca76ab0\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"get_db_health_metrics\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"service\\\": \\\"postgres\\\", \\\"start_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\\\", \\\"end_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\\\", \\\"limit\\\": 50}, \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"NO_DATA\\\"}, {\\\"call_id\\\": \\\"call-7fb045abd157463e96d1b6ac06b1cf1f\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"get_db_connections\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"service\\\": \\\"postgres\\\", \\\"start_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\\\", \\\"end_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\\\", \\\"limit\\\": 50}, \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"NO_DATA\\\"}]\", \"evidence_ids\": [], \"relation\": \"neutral\", \"confidence_qualifier\": \"unknown\", \"followup_question\": \"Choose an available service, window or evidence source.\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"gap-54346d3b09895b699da29f3c4ae90190a127735080bfd0331b4e7b8fc0028f3b\", \"task_id\": \"task-02-change-diff\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"role\": \"changes\", \"claim\": \"No evidence for this query; this is not proof of healthy behavior. [{\\\"call_id\\\": \\\"call-4a1a08c29d9544ee93955d548573d11e\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"query_changes\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"service\\\": null}, \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"NO_DATA\\\"}]\", \"evidence_ids\": [], \"relation\": \"neutral\", \"confidence_qualifier\": \"unknown\", \"followup_question\": \"Choose an available service, window or evidence source.\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"finding-eccc8385102f6be81618abda91ded173a3f4510b7599c783372d5e809ceb88a5\", \"task_id\": \"task-03-backend-runtime-metrics\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"claim\": \"The only supplied backend measurement is request_latency_ms=40 ms at 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z, and backend is recorded as depending on postgres, redis, and payment; no backend cpu_usage, memory_usage, thread_count, or error_rate telemetry is present, so backend-local resource saturation is neither observed nor ruled out by the available evidence.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"incident_1003-E-001\", \"incident_1003-T-backend\"], \"relation\": \"neutral\", \"confidence_qualifier\": \"unknown\", \"followup_question\": \"Are backend cpu_usage, memory_usage, thread_count, latency_p99, and error_rate metrics available and abnormal during 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z to 2026-10-01T13:00:00Z?\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"finding-24706761a1b832eb55814a4e6c6f04db28ef19e9b5875e4289e85916441197c7\", \"task_id\": \"task-04-gateway-backend-error-logs\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"claim\": \"Within the supplied log scope the only two records are incident_1003-E-002 (gateway, 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z) showing 'Request completed with HTTP 200' and incident_1003-E-003 (backend, 2026-10-01T12:00:14Z) showing 'Request processing exceeded deadline'; no gateway ERROR/CRITICAL records and no redis/payment/pool error text are present, so no downstream dependency failure or gateway-local fault is evidenced by the provided excerpts, while the backend deadline-exceeded record at T+14s is the only observed failure signal.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"incident_1003-E-002\", \"incident_1003-E-003\"], \"relation\": \"neutral\", \"confidence_qualifier\": \"weak\", \"followup_question\": \"Can gateway and backend logs for 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z be re-queried with no severity filter and contains-terms ('deadline','pool','redis','payment','timeout') to expose the true first-onset ERROR/CRITICAL records and their timestamps?\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"finding-816cedee6611c225d121bee9e148a770f38b7d8e8917b16bcdcb47e0f7e979d0\", \"task_id\": \"task-05-redis-runtime-metrics\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"claim\": \"The only observed record for redis is the topology entry incident_1003-T-redis stating that redis depends on no services; no redis-side latency, error_rate, or availability metric samples have been observed in this run, so redis runtime degradation is neither confirmed nor excluded and the redis_unavailable versus backend_resource_saturation discrimination remains unresolved on observed evidence. Data gaps (not evidence of health): [{\\\"call_id\\\": \\\"call-8b99844381da46fba8bf1766a415fe0f\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"query_metrics\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"service\\\": \\\"redis\\\", \\\"start_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\\\", \\\"end_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\\\", \\\"metric_names\\\": []}, \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"NO_DATA\\\"}]\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"incident_1003-T-redis\"], \"relation\": \"neutral\", \"confidence_qualifier\": \"unknown\", \"followup_question\": \"Do redis latency, error_rate, or availability metrics degrade during 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z while backend-local resource metrics stay normal, which would separate redis_unavailable from backend_resource_saturation?\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"finding-64b833cab853efa21997244d76b2a81b22b95c0b22245a8f83cbd3eb580838e4\", \"task_id\": \"task-06-payment-runtime-metrics\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"claim\": \"The only observed metric in scope is backend request_latency_ms=40 ms at 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z, which is within normal range and carries no payment-side signal; no payment external call latency or error-rate telemetry has been observed, so the payment dependency's runtime behavior during the window remains unknown. Data gaps (not evidence of health): [{\\\"call_id\\\": \\\"call-92f98202a8854419aa3a641352eb60fd\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"query_metrics\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"service\\\": \\\"payment\\\", \\\"metric_names\\\": [], \\\"start_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\\\", \\\"end_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\\\"}, \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"NO_DATA\\\"}]\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"incident_1003-E-001\"], \"relation\": \"neutral\", \"confidence_qualifier\": \"unknown\", \"followup_question\": \"What are payment external-call latency and error-rate values during 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z?\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"gap-e5c8ef439b8de08325677e6a5e5835dee785b3e2f2dd43a5f57bdcff324d8982\", \"task_id\": \"task-07-redis-error-logs\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"claim\": \"No evidence for this query; this is not proof of healthy behavior. [{\\\"call_id\\\": \\\"call-eeb84df7db4c4ca5911c68a811f3d5cd\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"query_logs\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"service\\\": \\\"redis\\\", \\\"start_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\\\", \\\"end_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\\\", \\\"limit\\\": 50}, \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"NO_DATA\\\"}]\", \"evidence_ids\": [], \"relation\": \"neutral\", \"confidence_qualifier\": \"unknown\", \"followup_question\": \"Choose an available service, window or evidence source.\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"finding-8080117d58698cccbcd67c76dd6eac5e536c27a777d097f0fe236225f44ebb77\", \"task_id\": \"task-08-payment-error-logs\", \"run_id\": \"run-ba7ea844bd6e4149abc999cd797587d8\", \"incident_id\": \"incident_1003\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"claim\": \"The only in-scope observed log record is a backend-origin deadline-exceeded entry with no service-internal or error-class detail (incident_1003-E-003, service=backend, observed_at=2026-10-01T12:00:14Z). No payment-sourced ERROR/CRITICAL record naming an external-call timeout or dependency unavailability was supplied for 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z, so the payment_external_timeout alternative is neither observed nor excluded by this evidence and the record is non-discriminating with respect to the surviving backend-side mechanism. Data gaps (not evidence of health): [{\\\"call_id\\\": \\\"call-83033d9bda404c88872d25cff1369281\\\", \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"query_logs\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"service\\\": \\\"payment\\\", \\\"start_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\\\", \\\"end_ts\\\": \\\"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\\\", \\\"limit\\\": 50}, \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"NO_DATA\\\"}]\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"incident_1003-E-003\"], \"relation\": \"neutral\", \"confidence_qualifier\": \"unknown\", \"followup_question\": \"Re-query the complete payment log stream for 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z without service-severity or contains filters: does any payment record name an external-call timeout, deadline, or dependency unavailability coinciding with the backend deadline-exceeded signal at 12:00:14Z?\"}], \"evidence_index\": {}, \"hypotheses\": [{\"hypothesis_id\": \"hyp-32a63ad13f743388bf95b6fc388791fe4b2369f6ac15c6a4124f9cf3b94a479d\", \"culprit_service\": \"backend\", \"failure_mode\": \"backend_resource_saturation\", \"support_ids\": [\"incident_1003-E-003\"], \"against_ids\": [], \"predicted_observations\": [\"backend deadline-exceeded records spanning multiple downstream dependencies rather than only payment-bound requests\", \"backend resource metrics (CPU, memory, thread/connection-pool utilisation) rising before the deadline-exceeded record at 12:00:14Z\", \"payment-side records absent or within normal bounds while backend-side latency grows\"], \"status\": \"OPEN\", \"open_questions\": [\"No backend resource or pool telemetry has been supplied for the incident window, so saturation cannot be confirmed or dismissed on observed mechanism.\", \"The deadline-exceeded record is a service-level symptom that does not by itself distinguish backend_resource_saturation from other backend-local failure modes (pool config regression, connection exhaustion, lock contention).\"]}, {\"hypothesis_id\": \"hyp-b645caa41a50357eeef8b5b0ddf65d66b43af94981a3be3ade6e10acfdcb3147\", \"culprit_service\": \"redis\", \"failure_mode\": \"redis_unavailable\", \"support_ids\": [\"incident_1003-T-backend\"], \"against_ids\": [], \"predicted_observations\": [\"Elevated redis latency or error_rate metrics during the incident window\", \"Redis availability or connection-refused signals co-occurring with backend deadline-exceeded symptoms\", \"redis-side error log records naming timeouts or unavailability preceding incident_1003-E-003 while backend-local resources remain normal\"], \"status\": \"OPEN\", \"open_questions\": [\"redis metric telemetry (query_metrics service=redis 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z) returned zero records, so redis-side runtime values remain entirely unobserved and the metric route is exhausted.\", \"Do redis ERROR/CRITICAL logs naming timeouts, connection refusals, or unavailability during 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z supply the remaining discriminating evidence for redis_unavailable?\"]}, {\"hypothesis_id\": \"hyp-08846516798c9ee4cb79fb1d1babf88c17c611c83e83c3e9ba21b1c768a0f030\", \"culprit_service\": \"payment\", \"failure_mode\": \"payment_external_timeout\", \"support_ids\": [\"incident_1003-T-backend\"], \"against_ids\": [], \"predicted_observations\": [\"backend deadline-exceeded records clustered on requests that transit payment while non-payment backend paths remain within deadline\", \"payment ERROR/CRITICAL records naming an external-call timeout or dependency unavailability within 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z\", \"payment-side upstream call latency or error-rate spike coinciding with or preceding the backend deadline-exceeded record at 12:00:14Z\"], \"status\": \"OPEN\", \"open_questions\": [\"No payment-sourced log or metric observation has been produced for the incident window, so a genuine payment external-call stall remains untested rather than refuted.\", \"Whether the backend deadline-exceeded record is downstream of a blocked payment dependency call or of a backend-internal stall cannot be decided without any payment-side record.\"]}], \"tasks\": [{\"task_id\": \"task-01-postgres-health\", \"role\": \"database\", \"question\": \"During the incident window, did postgres show connection exhaustion (active sessions approaching connection limits or connection acquisition failures), lock waits, or slow queries that could causally explain the observed latency and error rate on gateway/backend?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"get_db_connections\", \"get_db_active_sessions\", \"get_db_lock_waits\", \"get_db_slow_queries\", \"get_db_health_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"postgres\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"limit\": 50}, \"reason\": \"postgres is a shared dependency of gateway, backend, and payment, database tooling is enabled, and database_health_normal is reported false, making concrete postgres health signals the highest-value first check on a common-cause candidate.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Observable postgres metrics distinguish mechanisms: a rise in active sessions/connection counts or connection errors supports postgres_connection_exhaustion; growing lock waits without connection saturation supports postgres_lock_contention; elevated slow-query durations with normal connections supports postgres_slow_query. Uniformly normal DB health across all five checks would leave these mechanisms unsupported and shift weight to config/change or non-DB causes.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-02-change-diff\", \"role\": \"changes\", \"question\": \"Were there recent deployments, config changes, maintenance, or scaling events affecting gateway/backend/postgres/redis/payment settings (especially connection-pool or dependency configuration) shortly before or during the incident window?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_changes\", \"get_config_diff\"], \"filters\": {}, \"reason\": \"A pool/config regression or an unplanned change is a competing causal mechanism that would not necessarily surface in runtime database metrics; inspecting changes and config diffs is required before concluding evidence is insufficient.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"A change record whose timestamp precedes the latency/error onset and whose config diff alters pool size, timeouts, or dependency endpoints supports backend_pool_config_regression or redis/payment configuration causes; absence of any such change with a complete unfiltered query result leaves those mechanisms unsupported and favors a runtime-resource or database-side explanation.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-03-backend-runtime-metrics\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"During the incident window, did backend (and its runtime host) exhibit resource saturation \\u2014 elevated CPU, memory pressure, thread/connection saturation, or a latency/error-rate rise that is not attributable to a downstream dependency \\u2014 which could causally explain the observed gateway/backend latency and error rate?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\", \"get_dependencies\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"backend\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"metric_names\": [\"cpu_usage\", \"memory_usage\", \"thread_count\", \"latency_p99\", \"error_rate\"]}, \"reason\": \"postgres-side checks returned no data and the unfiltered change query was empty, so the next highest-value causal source is backend runtime telemetry: backend_resource_saturation is a listed taxonomy mechanism that would not appear in database or change records, and backend/gateway are the services exhibiting the symptom. get_dependencies is included to separate a backend-local resource fault from a downstream redis/payment dependency effect before concluding evidence is insufficient.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"A backend-local rise in CPU/memory/thread metrics co-occurring with the latency and error onset, with dependencies resolved and healthy, supports backend_resource_saturation; uniformly normal backend resource metrics with elevated dependency latency or unresolved/failed dependency calls shifts weight toward redis_unavailable or payment_external_timeout; normal backend resources with healthy dependencies leaves gateway-origin or unexamined mechanisms open and prevents a premature ABSTAIN.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-04-gateway-backend-error-logs\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"question\": \"During the incident window, what ERROR/CRITICAL log records were emitted by gateway and backend, and do they indicate an upstream connection-pool/config regression, a downstream redis or payment dependency failure, or a gateway-local fault preceding the latency and error rise?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_logs\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"gateway\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"severity\": \"ERROR\", \"limit\": 50}, \"reason\": \"Logs are an independent causal source not yet exercised in this incident: the database and change roles produced only gaps, so error text and chronology from gateway is needed to identify an observed failure mechanism rather than inferring root cause from an error string alone. gateway is chosen as the entry point of the observed latency/error window and its shared span with backend/payment\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Error records referencing dependency endpoints (redis/payment) with timestamps preceding the backend latency rise support redis_unavailable or payment_external_timeout; pool/timeout configuration or connection-acquisition errors at first-onset support backend_pool_config_regression; gateway-local errors with no downstream dependency references favor a gateway-origin fault. Absence of any error records in a complete scope leaves these mechanisms unsupported and defers to the metrics task.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-05-redis-runtime-metrics\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"During 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z, do redis latency, error_rate, or availability metrics degrade while backend-local resources remain normal, which would discriminate redis_unavailable from backend_resource_saturation?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\", \"get_dependencies\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"redis\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"metric_names\": []}, \"reason\": \"The redis_unavailable candidate is currently supported only by the backend->redis topology edge incident_1003-T-backend and no redis-side query exists anywhere in query_history, so redis runtime telemetry is the unobserved causal source that must be inspected before repeating unavailable backend resource telemetry; get_dependencies separates a redis-local fault from the backend-side mechanism.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Elevated redis latency, error_rate, or unavailability metrics co-occurring with the backend deadline-exceeded record incident_1003-E-003 while backend-local signals stay normal supports redis_unavailable; uniformly normal redis telemetry keeps backend_resource_saturation as the surviving mechanism and weakens the redis dependency alternative.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-06-payment-runtime-metrics\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"During 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z, does the payment dependency show elevated external call latency or error rate that could explain the backend deadline-exceeded record without backend-local saturation?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\", \"get_dependencies\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"payment\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"metric_names\": []}, \"reason\": \"payment_external_timeout rests only on the backend->payment topology edge incident_1003-T-backend and no payment-side query has been issued, so payment runtime telemetry is an unobserved causal source needed to separate a dependency stall from the backend-local mechanism before any FINALIZE/ABSTAIN is considered.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"A payment latency or error rise during the window supports payment_external_timeout; uniformly normal payment telemetry removes the payment alternative and leaves backend_resource_saturation as the surviving backend-side mechanism.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-07-redis-error-logs\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"question\": \"During 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z, do redis emit any ERROR/CRITICAL records naming timeouts, connection refusals, or unavailability that could causally explain the backend deadline-exceeded record incident_1003-E-003?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_logs\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"redis\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"severity\": \"ERROR\", \"contains\": \"timeout\", \"limit\": 50}, \"reason\": \"redis runtime metric telemetry (query_metrics service=redis) returned zero records, so the metric route to the redis_unavailable alternative is exhausted; error logs are an independent causal source not yet exercised for redis and are the remaining scope that can reveal an observed redis-side failure mechanism rather than repeating unavailable telemetry.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Timeout, connection-refused, or unavailability records emitted by redis that precede or coincide with incident_1003-E-003 support redis_unavailable; absence of any redis error records in a complete severity-filtered scope leaves the redis alternative unsupported and keeps backend_resource_saturation as the surviving mechanism.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-08-payment-error-logs\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"question\": \"During 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z, does payment emit any ERROR/CRITICAL records naming external call timeouts or unavailability that could explain the backend deadline-exceeded record incident_1003-E-003 without backend-local saturation?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_logs\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"payment\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"severity\": \"ERROR\", \"contains\": \"timeout\", \"limit\": 50}, \"reason\": \"payment runtime metric telemetry (query_metrics service=payment) returned zero records, so the metric probe into the payment_external_timeout alternative is exhausted; payment error logs are the unobserved independent source that can separate a genuine dependency stall from the backend-local mechanism without re-issuing empty telemetry.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"External-call timeout or unavailability records from payment coinciding with the backend deadline-exceeded signal support payment_external_timeout; absence of any payment error records in a complete scope removes the payment alternative and leaves backend_resource_saturation as the surviving backend-side mechanism.\"}], \"reviews\": [{\"target_hypothesis_id\": \"hyp-32a63ad13f743388bf95b6fc388791fe4b2369f6ac15c6a4124f9cf3b94a479d\", \"verdict\": \"insufficient\", \"contradictions\": [], \"requested_checks\": [{\"task_id\": \"ver-0009-redis-runtime-metrics\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"During 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z, do redis latency, error_rate, or availability metrics degrade while backend-local resources remain normal, which would discriminate redis_unavailable from backend_resource_saturation?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"redis\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"metric_names\": []}, \"reason\": \"The redis_unavailable candidate is currently supported only by the backend->redis topology edge (incident_1003-T-backend) and no redis-side query exists anywhere in query_history, so redis runtime telemetry is the unobserved causal source that must be inspected before repeating unavailable backend telemetry.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Elevated redis latency or error metrics co-occurring with the backend deadline-exceeded record while backend-local signals stay normal supports redis_unavailable; uniformly normal redis telemetry keeps backend_resource_saturation alive and weakens the dependency alternative.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"ver-0009-payment-external-latency\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"During 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z, does the payment dependency show elevated external call latency or error rate that could explain the backend deadline-exceeded record without backend-local saturation?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"payment\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"metric_names\": []}, \"reason\": \"payment_external_timeout rests only on the backend->payment topology edge (incident_1003-T-backend) and no payment-side query has been issued, so payment runtime telemetry is an unobserved causal source needed to separate a dependency stall from the backend-local mechanism.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"A payment latency or error rise during the window supports payment_external_timeout; uniformly normal payment telemetry leaves backend_resource_saturation as the surviving backend-side mechanism and removes the dependency alternatives.\"}], \"optional_checks\": [{\"task_id\": \"ver-0009-redis-payment-error-logs\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"question\": \"Do redis and payment emit any ERROR/CRITICAL log records in 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z-13:00:00Z that name timeouts or unavailability?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_logs\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"redis\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:00:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"severity\": \"ERROR\", \"limit\": 50}, \"reason\": \"Nonblocking corroboration for the dependency alternatives; not required for a verdict because the topology edge alone does not prove a dependency fault and the blocking metric checks carry the primary discriminator.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Timeout or unavailability records from redis/payment would corroborate a dependency fault; their absence would leave those mechanisms unsupported.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"ver-0009-backend-resource-metrics-recheck\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"If backend runtime telemetry becomes available, are cpu_usage, memory_usage, thread_count, latency_p99, or error_rate elevated during the incident window?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"backend\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:55:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T13:00:00Z\", \"metric_names\": [\"cpu_usage\", \"memory_usage\", \"thread_count\", \"latency_p99\", \"error_rate\"]}, \"reason\": \"Nonblocking corroboration for backend_resource_saturation; the prior backend metric query returned only incident_1003-E-001 (latency 40 ms), so this repeats potentially unavailable telemetry and is deferred to optional rather than blocking scope.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Elevated backend CPU/memory/thread or latency metrics co-occurring with the deadline-exceeded record support backend_resource_saturation; uniformly normal values weaken it.\"}], \"cited_evidence_ids\": [\"incident_1003-E-001\", \"incident_1003-E-002\", \"incident_1003-E-003\", \"incident_1003-T-backend\"], \"rationale\": \"The latest decision selects no hypothesis for FINALIZE (selected_hypothesis_id is null), so the best-grounded existing candidate is reviewed: hyp-32a63ad13... (backend_resource_saturation, culprit backend). It is the best grounded because its only support record i